# Production environment template for the web build. Copy to .env.production (Vite auto-loads
# this for `vite build --mode production`, which `npm run build` already uses by default) and
# fill in the real value, or set VITE_API_URL directly in your hosting provider's build-time
# environment variables — never commit a real .env.production with values other than this
# template's placeholders.

# Must be a real https:// URL — the deployed backend's public origin plus /api. A mixed-content
# or CORS failure at runtime almost always means this still points at localhost or http://.
VITE_API_URL=https://<your-production-backend-domain>/api
